# Everything the build does not need, plus everything it must never see.
#
# Two jobs. Keeping the context small is the minor one; keeping secrets and user
# data out of the image is the point. A COPY of the repo root would otherwise
# pull in the SQLite database (usernames, bcrypt hashes, cognitive scores),
# uploaded voice recordings and photos, and the VAPID private key — baked into
# every layer, readable by anyone who pulls the image, and undeleteable because
# layers are immutable.

# === Secrets and user data — NEVER in an image ==============================
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

backend/db/
backend/app/db/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/cognisense.db
**/cognisense.db-journal
**/cognisense.db-wal
**/cognisense.db-shm

# Uploaded media.
**/audio/
**/reminders/
**/user_photos/

# === Rebuilt inside the image ==============================================
# Checkpoints are retrained by the Dockerfile; a stale host copy would be
# silently baked in instead.
backend/app/ml/checkpoints/

# node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` in the web stage. Copying the host
# copy would be slower AND wrong — host binaries may not match the build image.
**/node_modules/
web_app/dist/

# === Python cruft ==========================================================
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/*.egg-info/

# === Not needed at runtime =================================================
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
backend/tests/
backend/results/
docs/
desktop_app/
**/README.md
!README.md
**/*.log

# === Editor / OS ===========================================================
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
